load @term/seed/code/group/homomorphism
  find group-homomorphism

# The kernel of a group homomorphism: the set of elements the homomorphism sends to the identity. It is always a normal
# subgroup of the source, and the source quotiented by the kernel is isomorphic to the image (the first isomorphism
# theorem). The kernel measures how far the homomorphism is from being injective: it is injective exactly when the
# kernel is trivial. The form carries the homomorphism whose kernel this is.
form homomorphism-kernel
  link map, like group-homomorphism
